    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d305">

                <pb facs="0491" n="397" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg397"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.945/1115: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Woods</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-05-28T17:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 28, 1924—5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 28—12:23
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>126. My number [<hi rendition="#italic">114</hi>], May 23, 6 p.m.<anchor n="57"
                        xml:id="d305-f1"/> I understand that the Cabinet at a meeting held this
                    morning approved the draft of <pb facs="0492" n="398" xml:id="pg398"/> an
                    instruction to Hanihara to “lodge a solemn protest.” An official statement in
                    this connection to be issued this afternoon will be cabled by the Associated
                    Press.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Woods</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
